cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Shredding cost: what physical storage layout does to write cost and index
  freshness in document databases
message: >-
  If you cite a figure from this repository, please read LIMITATIONS.md
  first and cite the measurement identifier (Mxx) alongside the number,
  so that the regime the number belongs to travels with it.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Leconte
    given-names: David
repository-code: https://github.com/davidleconte/shredding-cost-hcd-mongodb
abstract: >-
  An adversarial self-verification of a technical article comparing the
  physical storage layout of IBM DataStax HCD 2.0.6 (Data API v1.0.33) and
  MongoDB 8.x. Seven measurement campaigns, 23 numbered measurements, with
  the raw JSON evidence, the probe source, an adversarial audit of the
  dossier's own integrity, and the points at which the measurements
  contradicted the article they were written to verify.
keywords:
  - document database
  - storage engine
  - Apache Cassandra
  - DataStax HCD
  - MongoDB
  - storage-attached index
  - read-modify-write
  - benchmark methodology
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
date-released: '2026-09-18'
